{"agent":"close-brules","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`rule_inventory` accepts `agent` and never uses it: `RI.inventory(repo)` is called with only the repo path. `rule_inventory(repo, agent=\"cursor\")` therefore returns the same census as `rule_inventory(repo)`, so a caller that asks for one agent's always-loaded cost cannot get it from this API.","digest":"be3673093b26f0ff","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/rulesinv.py:11","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/rulesinv.py:11"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"`scan_rule_files` freezes `kind` and `load` on the first pattern that hits a path, so the \"rule glob wins\" branch never runs when a command directory is expanded first. `_surfaces` follows `HR.load()` order and emits `commands.dir` entries as `KIND_COMMAND`. If that harness is registered before one whose `instructions.reads` also matches the file (for example commands dir `.claude/commands/` then a read `.claude/commands/*.md` of `ship.md` with `alwaysApply: true`), the row stays `command` / `on request`. Later rule agents are only appended to `loaded_by`. `always_bytes` drops the file (`kind != KIND_COMMAND` is false), `_restatements` skips it, and `doctor_note` ignores it, so an always-loaded project rule is reported as an on-request command and a split fleet can be silent.","digest":"db13e1bb4881a28f","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/rulesinv.py:scan_rule_files","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/rulesinv.py:scan_rule_files"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"`_SKIP_DIRS` is applied only on trailing-slash `rglob` walks. Any `reads` pattern containing `*`, `?`, or `[` goes through `repo.glob` with no skip. Given `worktrees/other/.cursor/rules/always.md` (no frontmatter) and a read such as `**/.cursor/rules/*.md`, that foreign copy is inventoried, classified always-loaded, and added to `always_bytes` / `loaded_by`. The same happens for `node_modules` and `.venv`. The comment says those trees are not this project's rules; the glob path still counts them.","digest":"75b56d4bac1c8afb","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/rulesinv.py:_expand","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/rulesinv.py:_expand"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":20845,"diff_sha":"d0a370e63032e8baa7e290c68ac38500f8d05ba13b70524c047bd2f1758df10a","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/B-rules-inventory","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":151.1,"excluded_bytes":1608,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["README.md"],"family":"xai","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"2bf4d338d7fbe7df","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/B-rules-inventory.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261111T103932Z-b2c42d97.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4],"reviewed_head":"d4940a6d1410f906e61afe3053b6da5eaab13785","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 80c329bdfb794c44cc0205fdd9b25d981d979691","ddflow/api/rulesinv.py":"100644 ad222cddbe55a04e62394f1a0065fe108b23deb1","ddflow/services/rulesinv.py":"100644 650928bb7245b8f8394036adee6c583c10f91c6a","ddflow/surfaces/declared/rules.py":"100644 a16f6f5daf3909d7124467874bffe758e36a05e8","tests/test_rules_inventory.py":"100644 81acbed14a894a0849de6993a686ce7b166c558b"},"reviewer":"grok-4.7","reviewer_digest":"1857ec352c55ee94","reviewer_families":["google","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/api/rulesinv.py:11","ddflow/services/rulesinv.py:scan_rule_files","ddflow/services/rulesinv.py:_expand"],"tree_sha":"d4940a6d1410+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"3 finding(s)"},"id":"e0b9753acad47edbab8f02d07","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":173045,"schema":1,"subject":"B-rules-inventory","ts":"2026-11-11T10:42:04.411514Z"}
